MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: aa9506f8b8c580c448622cdfc193780a, type: 3}
  m_Name: Case1_Clocktower
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CaseDefinition
  CaseId: clocktower
  Number: 1
  Title: The 3:15 Escapement
  Location: "The Clocktower Gear Room  \xB7  3:15 AM"
  SceneName: Clocktower
  MenuBlurb: Inventor Arthur Vance lies beneath the fallen pendulum of the town clock.
    The great clock stopped at 3:15. Was it an accident?
  Intro: 'The great clock of Ashgrove stopped at 3:15 this morning, and half the
    town woke to the silence. Inventor Arthur Vance was found in the gear room beneath
    the fallen pendulum.


    The constable calls it an accident. You don''t. Search
    the tower, question anyone lurking in the shadows, and name the killer before
    the trail goes cold.'
  Clues:
  - Id: CLUE_PENDULUM_PIN
    Riddle: 'I held the heart that kept the town''s time, till a shaking hand pulled
      me free. You can''t lift me: look where the brass rod meets the big wheel.'
    Tip: Not everything worth seeing can be carried. Go to the fallen pendulum and
      look where the rod meets the great wheel.
  - Id: CLUE_CHISEL
    Riddle: Where the moon spills silver on the boards, a rusty tooth lies forgotten.
      Look down in the light from the big clock face.
    Tip: Moonlight shows more than it hides. Check the floor inside the glow from
      the clock face, and look down.
  - Id: CLUE_LOGBOOK
    Riddle: Where an old man warmed his hands by the glass, his words wait for anyone
      who passes. Follow the little orange glow.
    Tip: The night watchman sat by a window to keep warm. Follow the little orange
      glow.
  - Id: CLUE_PRESCRIPTION
    Riddle: Six little rooms sit on the desk. Five hold rolled-up scrolls, and one
      holds a doctor's folded promise that somebody broke.
    Tip: Vance kept his papers in pigeonholes. Not every one of them is empty.
  - Id: CLUE_TEACUP
    Riddle: Fallen but not broken, cold but once warm. I'm on the floor by the desk,
      and I've a ring on my plate that isn't mine.
    Tip: Someone knocked something off that desk tonight. Look at the floor beside
      it.
  - Id: CLUE_LETTER
    Riddle: Sealed in red and full of family spite, I lie on the slope where he drew
      at night. Left side, detective.
    Tip: There's a letter on the desk with a red seal. Family business, and nasty
      business.
  - Id: CLUE_POCKET_WATCH
    Riddle: I've got hands but I can't clap, and someone told me to stop. I'm lying
      on the sloped desk, near the edge, waitin' to be picked up.
    Tip: His pocket watch is on the sloping desk, near the front edge. A watchmaker
      doesn't stop a watch for nothing.
  - Id: CLUE_DESK_LAMP
    Riddle: I've a neck like a swan and a hat like a bell. I'm bowing my head to
      show you what I saw. Look on the desk's back shelf.
    Tip: Look at the brass lamp on the back shelf of the desk, and at what it's pointing
      at.
  - Id: CLUE_APOTHECARY_VIAL
    Riddle: Small and corked and nearly dry, I stand on the shelf beside the bright
      one. What I held put a man to sleep for good.
    Tip: A small corked bottle stands on the desk's back shelf beside the lamp. Read
      the label.
  CluesRequiredToAccuse: 5
  MaxAccusations: 3
  Questions:
  - Prompt: Who poisoned Arthur Vance?
    Options:
    - Dr. Elias Haze
    - Margaret Vance
    - Tobias Crane
    - 'No one: an accident'
    CorrectIndex: 0
  - Prompt: When did the poison take hold?
    Options:
    - 2:40 AM
    - 3:03 AM
    - 3:10 AM
    - 3:15 AM
    CorrectIndex: 1
  - Prompt: How was he killed?
    Options:
    - Aconite in his tonic
    - Crushed by the pendulum
    - Gears sabotaged to fall
    - Poisoned wax seal
    CorrectIndex: 0
  - Prompt: Who stopped the great clock at 3:15?
    Options:
    - Arthur Vance himself
    - Dr. Elias Haze
    - Tobias Crane
    - Margaret Vance
    CorrectIndex: 0
  SolutionText: 'Dr. Elias Haze came up the tower at 2:40 with Vance''s evening tonic,
    and he had altered the dose from 10 drops to 40. The bottle was <b>aconite</b>,
    labelled in his own hand. They shared tea, then Haze took his cup and fled at
    3:10.


    At <b>3:03</b> Vance felt his hands go numb and understood. A horologist
    to the last, he stopped his watch to mark the moment, then turned his lamp onto
    a note. With minutes left he drew the pendulum''s pin himself. The great clock
    stopped at <b>3:15</b>, waking the whole town before Haze could return to tidy
    up.


    Margaret''s threat was only angry words: she was at the gala until
    3:30. Crane''s chisel marks were months old, and he had left at 11:02.'
  FailLine: Your last accusation falls apart. By dawn, Dr. Haze is on the 6:15 train
    to the coast.
  TopRankName: Master of the Escapement
  WrenCallOut: Psst... over here, detective. By the window.
  WrenIntro: Easy. I'm not here to hurt you. I watch this tower for people who pay
    well, and tonight nobody paid me to look away. So I looked.
  WrenWhoAmI: Call me Wren. Names are expensive, so that one's a gift. I keep an
    eye on Vance's work for a client who wanted his designs. Dead men don't sell
    blueprints, so I want his killer caught as much as you do.
  WrenSuspectsLine: Three people had reason to want Vance gone. Pick one.
  Suspects:
  - Name: Dr. Elias Haze
    Role: the physician
    Intel: Town doctor. Treats half the council, and owes the bank twice what he
      earns. Vance found out Haze was watering down patients' medicine and pocketing
      the difference. He was going to the constable on Monday.
  - Name: Margaret Vance
    Role: the niece
    Intel: Hot temper, empty purse. She inherits if the will stands. But she spent
      tonight dancing at the Founders' Gala. Half the town saw her there, and the
      watchman writes everything down.
  - Name: Tobias Crane
    Role: the rival
    Intel: 'Vance''s old apprentice. Swears Vance stole his escapement design. Loud,
      petty, and sloppy with his tools: he leaves them everywhere and never cleans
      them.'
  DeductionTips:
  - 'You''ve got every piece. Now check alibis: two of your suspects were nowhere
    near this room when it mattered. The watchman''s book says who.'
  - The poison took hold before the clock stopped. A watchmaker would mark that moment
    on the thing he trusts most.
  - Ask who was in this room after Haze ran down the stairs at 3:10. Only one man.
    And he was dying, but not finished.
  WrenSolved: Nicely done, detective. Haze will run, or hang. Either way my client
    will be pleased. You never saw me.
  FinchCallOut: Oi! Detective! Behind the gears. Quick, before the coppers see me!
  FinchIntro: Name's Finch. I run messages for Wren, and for anyone with a coin.
    But for you, riddles are free! Wren charges for tips. I don't. Mine are just
    harder to crack.
  FinchWitness: I was hidin' on the stair. Somebody came down past me in a proper
    hurry. Didn't see a face, but they'd no hat, and their bag clinked like little
    glass bottles. Then BONG! The whole tower shook and the clock stopped.
  FinchSolved: You did it! I'll run the news to every street in town. First edition,
    no charge!
